Z||000000||Haze_Performance||10-02-2000||04:01 PM||||I know the Auto Trans Codes are F17 = 2.84 and GT7 = 3.33. Im tring to decode the RPO codes under the hood. I bought a 1985 Pontiac Dealer Order Steet but all the codes are not on it. How do I decode the rest (like the trans) ? <P>There are 47 codes on the sticker. My order sheet only decodes about 15.<P>TIA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Carl<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif">  <P><B>Website's<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A><P>                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||7
Z||000001||baldlobo||10-02-2000||04:31 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Haze_Performance:<BR><B>I know the Auto Trans Codes are F17 = 2.84 and GT7 = 3.33. Im tring to decode the RPO codes under the hood. I bought a 1985 Pontiac Dealer Order Steet but all the codes are not on it. How do I decode the rest (like the trans) ? <P>There are 47 codes on the sticker. My order sheet only decodes about 15.<P>TIA   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Carl<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>you goto <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/RPOlist.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/RPOlist.html</A> <BR>it has all of the rpo codes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Haze_Performance||10-02-2000||07:36 PM||||Thank You for the link  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif">  <P><B>Website's<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A><P>                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||14
Z||000003||theogre||10-02-2000||08:13 PM||||from an update to a cave article not yet posted...<P>Final Drive Ratios<BR>All TH125 transmissions are essentially the same except for the final drive gears. The following RPO codes apply to TH125c and 440 T4 transmission final drive gears.<P>FP3, FW2, FW9, F47, F90 = 3.06 <P>F16, F17, F62, F75 = 2.84<P>F77, F79, GX3 = 3.33<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Haze_Performance||10-02-2000||08:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by theogre:<BR><B>from an update to a cave article not yet posted...<P>Final Drive Ratios<BR>All TH125 transmissions are essentially the same except for the final drive gears. The following RPO codes apply to TH125c and 440 T4 transmission final drive gears.<P>FP3, FW2, FW9, F47, F90 = 3.06 <P>F16, F17, F62, F75 = 2.84<P>F77, F79, GX3 = 3.33<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>At <A HREF="http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/RPOlist.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.homestead.com/fiero2m4/RPOlist.html</A> <BR>it says "F75 Transaxle, final drive, is a 3.18 ratio".<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif">  <P><B>Website's<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A><P>                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||5
Z||000005||mrfiero||10-02-2000||09:47 PM||||Does anyone know how to tell which final drive  a tranny has once it's out of the car?<P>I ask this because I picked up a tranny (it was free!) and I have no idea what it came out of or what final drive it has.  I do know it was not from a Fiero....the VIN is all wrong for that.<P>TIA.||||reg||5
Z||000006||Haze_Performance||10-03-2000||01:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B>I do know it was not from a Fiero....the VIN is all wrong for that.<P>TIA.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Whats the VIN #? If you run it through carfax you can tell what car its out of.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2d_00010aa3.gif">  <P><B>Website's<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.WS6Fiero.com" TARGET=_blank>www.WS6Fiero.com</A><P>                  <A HREF="http://www.hazeperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>www.HazePerformance.com </A></B>||||reg||5
Z||000007||mrfiero||10-03-2000||01:39 AM||||It's only a partial VIN stamped on the tranny......I wish I knew the entire thing.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||10-03-2000||09:14 AM||||there should be a metal tag on the tranny. number on that tag can be run thru the dealler and they may be able to tell you.<P>The number I posted above are directly out of a GM TSB. I'll check them against a full GM RPO list when I get home, but I'm pretty sure they are correct. (The full list from GM was about 20 pages.)||||reg||1
